---
import PageLayout from "@/layouts/Base";

const meta = {
  title: "Privacy Policy - Evenzero",
  description:
    "Learn about Evenzero and Suraj Sharma - Weapons-grade software engineering and distributed systems expertise since 2000. Trusted by Goldman Sachs, MIT, Palantir, and Y Combinator startups.",
};
---

<PageLayout meta={meta}>
  <div class="privacy">
    <div class="space-y-6 bg-bgColor p-2 opacity-90 shadow">
      <div
        class="flex flex-col gap-8 rounded-lg border border-bgColor p-6 md:p-8"
      >
        <div class="space-y-4 pb-4">
          <h1 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold uppercase text-center">
            Evenzero Privacy Policy
          </h1>
          
          <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 italic text-center">
            Effective Date: 10th Of April, 2026
          </p>
        </div>

        <p class="text-justify pt-2">
          Evenzero ("we," "our," or "us") builds software products designed to respect user privacy by default. This Privacy Policy applies to all applications, services, and software products published by Evenzero, now and in the future (collectively, the "Services").
        </p>

        <hr class="border-gray-300" />
        <br />

        <section class="space-y-3">
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">1. Core Principle</h2>
          <p class="text-justify">
            We design our Services to minimize or eliminate the collection of personal data. Wherever possible, data remains on your device or is handled by trusted platform providers such as Google.
          </p>
        </section>

        <br />
        <hr class="border-gray-300" />
        <br />

        <section class="space-y-3">
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">2. Information We Do Not Collect</h2>
          <p class="text-justify">
            Evenzero does not directly collect, store, or process personal information such as:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-1 ml-4">
            <li>Name, email address, or phone number</li>
            <li>Messages, notes, or user-generated content</li>
            <li>Location data</li>
            <li>Contacts or media files</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="text-justify">
            Your data remains on your device or within systems managed by third-party platform providers you choose to use.
          </p>
        </section>

        <br />
        <hr class="border-gray-300" />
        <br />

        <section class="space-y-3">
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">3. Authentication and Account Data</h2>
          <p class="text-justify">
            Some Services may use third-party authentication providers (such as Google Sign-In).
          </p>
          <p class="text-justify">In such cases:</p>
          <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-1 ml-4">
            <li>Authentication is handled entirely by the provider</li>
            <li>Evenzero does not store or manage your login credentials</li>
            <li>We may receive basic account identifiers (e.g., a user ID or email) only as required to enable functionality, but we do not independently store or exploit this information</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <br />
        <hr class="border-gray-300" />
        <br />

        <section class="space-y-3">
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">4. Payments and Transactions</h2>
          <p class="text-justify">
            All payments are processed through platform providers such as Google Play.
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-1 ml-4">
            <li>Evenzero does not collect or store payment details (e.g., card numbers, billing information)</li>
            <li>Payment data is handled entirely by the platform provider under their own privacy policies</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <br />
        <hr class="border-gray-300" />
        <br />

        <section class="space-y-3">
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">5. Data Storage and Processing</h2>
          <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-1 ml-4">
            <li>User data is stored locally on your device unless explicitly stated otherwise within a specific product</li>
            <li>If cloud features are used, data may be stored using trusted infrastructure providers (e.g., Google services) under their security and privacy frameworks</li>
            <li>Evenzero does not maintain independent centralized databases of user personal data</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <br />
        <hr class="border-gray-300" />
        <br />

        <section class="space-y-3">
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">6. Analytics, Tracking, and Advertising</h2>
          <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-1 ml-4">
            <li>We do not use advertising networks</li>
            <li>We do not run third-party ads</li>
            <li>We do not track users across apps or services for profiling or behavioral advertising</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="text-justify">
            Limited technical data (such as crash reports or performance diagnostics) may be collected automatically by platform providers (e.g., Google Play services) to maintain app stability. This data is not used by Evenzero to identify users.
          </p>
        </section>

        <br />
        <hr class="border-gray-300" />
        <br />

        <section class="space-y-3">
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">7. Children's Privacy</h2>
          <p class="text-justify">
            Our Services may be used by individuals of all ages, including minors.
          </p>
          <p class="text-justify">
            We do not knowingly collect personal data from children. Since we do not directly collect personal information, we minimize risks associated with children's data.
          </p>
          <p class="text-justify">
            Parents or guardians who have concerns may contact us using the information below.
          </p>
        </section>

        <br />
        <hr class="border-gray-300" />
        <br />

        <section class="space-y-3">
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">8. User Rights and Control</h2>
          <p class="text-justify">You retain full control over your data:</p>
          <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-1 ml-4">
            <li>You can delete app data at any time by uninstalling the app or clearing storage</li>
            <li>Any data stored with third-party providers (e.g., Google) can be managed through your account with those providers</li>
            <li>Since we do not maintain independent user databases, we do not retain personal data after you stop using the Services</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <br />
        <hr class="border-gray-300" />
        <br />

        <section class="space-y-3">
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">9. Third-Party Services</h2>
          <p class="text-justify">
            Our Services may rely on third-party platforms such as Google for:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-1 ml-4">
            <li>Authentication</li>
            <li>Payments</li>
            <li>Infrastructure or storage</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="text-justify">
            These providers operate under their own privacy policies. We encourage you to review them.
          </p>
        </section>

        <br />
        <hr class="border-gray-300" />
        <br />

        <section class="space-y-3">
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">10. Data Security</h2>
          <p class="text-justify">
            We follow a minimal-data approach to reduce risk exposure. By avoiding centralized data collection, we significantly limit the surface area for unauthorized access.
          </p>
          <p class="text-justify">
            However, no system is completely secure, and users should take appropriate steps to protect their own devices and accounts.
          </p>
        </section>

        <br />
        <hr class="border-gray-300" />
        <br />

        <section class="space-y-3">
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">11. Changes to This Policy</h2>
          <p class="text-justify">
            We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time to reflect changes in technology, legal requirements, or our Services.
          </p>
          <p class="text-justify">
            Updates will be reflected by revising the "Effective Date." Continued use of the Services constitutes acceptance of the updated policy.
          </p>
        </section>

        <br />
        <hr class="border-gray-300" />
        <br />

        <section class="space-y-3">
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">12. Contact Us</h2>
          <p class="text-justify">
            If you have any questions or concerns about this Privacy Policy, you may contact us at:
          </p>
          <p class="ml-4">
            <strong>Email:</strong> suraj@evenzero.in <br />
            <strong>Organization:</strong> Evenzero
          </p>
        </section>

        <br />
        <hr class="border-gray-300" />
        <br />

        <section class="space-y-3">
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">13. Scope</h2>
          <p class="text-justify">
            This Privacy Policy applies to all current and future products, unless a specific product provides a separate, more detailed privacy policy.
          </p>
        </section>

        <br />
        <hr class="border-gray-300" />
        <br />

        <p class="text-justify font-medium pt-4">
          By using Evenzero Services, you acknowledge that you have read and understood this Privacy Policy.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</PageLayout>